l":"https://api.github.com/repos/stranske/Ready/actions/runs/34862159566/rerun","previous_attempt_url":null,"workflow_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stranske/Ready/actions/workflows/357348538","head_commit":{"id":"2dd52d56932de83b4f0f5c02c4274802ebd7dd31","tree_id":"8e1d0d4f6a210160cd0ed49ebd143d074ffcd3ba","message":"feat(publication): enforce research safety scan in required Gate (#569)\n\n* feat(publication): enforce research safety scan in required Gate\n\n* fix(publication): address Copilot review on workflow_call permissions and allowlist self-bypass\n\nMove contents:read under the publication-safety job so workflow_call from Gate\ndoes not hit reusable-workflow startup_failure. Reject .publication-allow as an\nallowlist target and add regression coverage for the self-allowlisted bypass case.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* fix(publication): move allowlist outside sync tree and add OSError tests\n\nRelocate .publication-allow to repo root so reviewed exceptions survive\nresearch-program mirror sync. Scan the allowlist explicitly, and add\ndeterministic fail-closed tests for Path.walk and read_bytes errors.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* chore: nudge PR synchronize after allowlist relocation push\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* fix(publication): prepare safe evidence copies before mirror publication\n\n* fix(publication): inspect decoded JSON strings before export\n\n* fix(publication): reject incomplete keys and duplicate JSON objects\n\n* fix(publication): reject non-finite JSON numbers before export\n\nFail closed when decoded JSON/JSONL contains NaN, Infinity, or overflowed\nfloats so redact_value cannot emit non-standard JSON. Add JSON and JSONL\nregression tests that prove earlier queued files remain untouched.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* chore(codex-keepalive): apply updates (PR #569)\n\n* chore(codex-keepalive): apply updates (PR #569)\n\n* chore(keepalive): reset runner-dispatch debounce\n\nThe keepalive runner-dispatch debounce is keyed on (head_sha, provider). The prior\ncodex run on this head exited reporting success while its sandbox had actually failed\n(bwrap: loopback: Failed RTM_NEWADDR), so it recorded a completed dispatch with zero\ntasks done. Every later dispatch then returned duplicate-completed, and the only thing\nthat clears that key is a new head commit -- which only the agent that is being refused\ncould produce. This content-identical commit breaks that deadlock.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(keepalive): reset runner-dispatch debounce\n\nThe keepalive runner-dispatch debounce is keyed on (head_sha, provider). The prior\ncodex run on this head exited reporting success while its sandbox had actually failed\n(bwrap: loopback: Failed RTM_NEWADDR), so it recorded a completed dispatch with zero\ntasks done. Every later dispatch then returned duplicate-completed, and the only thing\nthat clears that key is a new head commit -- which only the agent that is being refused\ncould produce. This content-identical commit breaks that deadlock.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(keepalive): reset runner-dispatch debounce\n\nThe keepalive runner-dispatch debounce is keyed on (head_sha, provider). The prior\ncodex run on this head exited reporting success while its sandbox had actually failed\n(bwrap: loopback: Failed RTM_NEWADDR), so it recorded a completed dispatch with zero\ntasks done. Every later dispatch then returned duplicate-completed, and the only thing\nthat clears that key is a new head commit -- which only the agent that is being refused\ncould produce. This content-identical commit breaks that deadlock.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(codex-keepalive): apply updates (PR #569)\n\n* fix(publication): reject non-regular files in preparation instead of hanging\n\nprepare_copy() called read_bytes() on every walked filename without checking it is a\nregular file. read_bytes() on a FIFO blocks forever waiting for a writer, so a staging\ntree containing one hangs preparation rather than being refused by it.\n\ncheck_publication_safety.py already rejects non-regular files. Preparation disagreeing\nwith the scanner means the stricter of the two is the one that never gets to run, which\nis the worst way for a safety pair to differ.\n\nDeliberate-break gate: removing the is_file() check makes\ntest_preparation_rejects_a_named_pipe_instead_of_hanging hang until killed (verified at a\n60s timeout); restoring it passes in 0.11s.\n\nFound by adversarial review of this PR.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore: remove generated coverage database from publication PR\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: stranske <tim@stranskemo.com>","timestamp":"2026-09-14T15:26:23Z","author":{"name":"stranske","email":"stranske@gmail.com"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com"}},"repository":{"id":1169688587,"node_id":"R_kgDORbgICw","name":"Ready","full_name":"stranske/Ready","private":false,"owner":{"login":"stranske","id":23046322,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDQ2MzIy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23046322?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stranske","html_url":"https://github.com/stranske","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stranske/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stranske/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stranske/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stranske/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stranske/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stransk